The fixture binds 53 imports, prints W32A16-NPP-OK and exits 78 with no TODO
fall-through and no fault.  The new REAL slices run in this same boot: the
DeferWindowPos batch is deferred then flushed (GetClientRect before/after), the
icon round-trip builds and splits an HICON, wsprintfW formats byte-exact, and
the two fail-clean stubs return their documented errors.  The offline updater
arm is visible: WinVerifyTrust answers TRUST_E_NOSIGNATURE (never "signed OK")
and the SENSAPI reachability probe reports offline (RST).

--- a bug this REAL boot caught (and the fix) ---
The FIRST real boot of this twin did NOT pass -- it page-faulted:

    W32-SEH-UNHANDLED code=0xc0000005 pc=0x4002af8b   (inside w32run, not the guest)
    [thread] '/apps/w32run' (tid 8) exited (code=139)

The fault was in USER32!wsprintfW.  W32ABI is __attribute__((ms_abi)) on
x86_64, so the guest calls the bound wsprintfW pointer with the Microsoft x64
varargs convention -- but the ms_abi twin walked its arguments with <stdarg.h>'s
va_list, which is the SysV register-save-area walker.  It read the varargs from
the wrong slots and dereferenced a garbage %s pointer.  The host sysv twin
(exercised by test_w32_a2/a9 under ASan/UBSan) never hit this because it is a
plain sysv function called the sysv way -- ONLY a real in-guest boot exercises
the ms_abi entry, so this was invisible to the host suite and to a merely
"described" boot receipt.  Fix: the ms_abi twin now uses __builtin_ms_va_list /
__builtin_ms_va_start / __builtin_va_arg / __builtin_ms_va_end
(w32/src/kernel32_loc.c, w32_user32_wsprintfW).  After the fix the boot is the
clean transcript above.  This is the lesson W32A-16 documents: an ms_abi
variadic export cannot be validated by a sysv host twin alone.

--- honest non-goals (human-run, framebuffer required) ---
The full Notepad++ receipt is human-run and pasted back hash-verified: the
Scintilla text render with syntax colours, the tab-switch pixels, the
Find/Replace dialog UI, the three shipped plugins' menu entries, drag-drop add
from the compositor (the GUI_EVT_DROP → WM_DROPFILES path W32A-11 already
proved end to end), and minimise-to-tray shown as a live compositor
notification.  Those need a framebuffer and a pixel oracle and are out of this
gate's automatable scope by design (named in docs/w32app_receipts.md #notepad++).
